Z||000004||California Kid||12-19-2001||06:23 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Joe Torma:<BR><B>I may want to get a license to make and sell all sorts of badges/logos/emblems of GM brands.<P>Nobody will care about the Fiero stuff, but if I want to go nuts, I don't want to get sued.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><BR>Send Rodney Dickman a pm, he sells items with the Logo on them, and might have some insight on this matter. I don't think the Fiero items will be an issue, but GM still owns the Logo and Brand Identification.<P>||||reg||1
Z||000005||8Ball||12-19-2001||11:20 PM||||  <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR><BR>I'm still trying to figure away to get into tier computer. haha Wouldn't that be great. I could spend days making a list of what is still available. I think the dealers are getting tired of me hanging out at the parts desk. Dave<P>[/b]<HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>I do all the Computer Service work for the dealerships around here. Unfortunately you cannot get into gm's computers.<P>They have to lease there servers from GM. Then in order to get into GM's Database for schematics, parts, manuals, or what ever, The leased server has to make a connection to the database. All done on private lines with no outside access available.<P>I already thought of it   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"><P><BR>(edited because I replied to the wrong post)<p>[This message has been edited by 8Ball (edited 12-19-2001).]||||reg||1
